=========================================
README for bkgstats_ts

Time series plotting tool:
    Generate time series of daily Mean Absolute Error (MAE) 
    between experiment background forecasts and a reference dataset
    for SST, SSH, or SEAICE
=========================================

--- How to run:

1. Add the following files to the /src directory (this only needs to be done once):

	On HERA:
		/scratch1/NCEPDEV/da/Katherine.Lukens/NSST/data/soca_gridspec.nc
		/scratch1/NCEPDEV/da/common/validation/oceanmask_global_0.25deg.20221025.xesmf_nearest_s2d.nc

2. In RUN_PLOT.time_series.daily.bash, set the following parameters:

        yyyyS, mmS, ddS ....... Start date (year, month, day)
        yyyyE, mmE, ddE ....... End date (year, month, day)
        variable .............. variable to plot: SST, SSH, SEAICE
        reference ............. reference dataset: ostia (SST or SEAICE), copernicus (SSH)
        oceans ................ ocean region to plot: Global, Atlantic, Pacific, Indian, Arctic, Southern
        account ............... HPC account
        qos ................... HPC QOS
        partition ............. HPC partition
        timelimit ............. HPC max time for job
        ntasks ................ HPC number of tasks (should = 1)

3. Run the tool:

	./RUN_PLOT.time_series.daily.bash

--- To add a new experiment for plotting:

1. cd src

2. In MAIN_PLOT.time_series.MAE.py, add the experiment path, experiment name, and a unique colorname to 
   the end of the following lists, respectively:
	
	exptpaths ............. add new experiment path
        exptnames ............. add new experiment name
        colors ................ add line color name for the new experiment

   NOTE: Add a comma to the end of the previous item in each of the above lists.

3. cd ..

4. ./RUN_PLOT.time_series.daily.bash


